al R+9 seat.", "watch": "Any additional public polling or a late shift in the national environment could push the race toward a true tossup, while a refocus on district fundamentals would widen Boebert's edge.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Lauren Boebert (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Lauren Boebert seeks reelection in a Colorado district that leans Republican by about nine points, a structural advantage in a midterm environment that otherwise favors Democrats. Challenger Eileen Laubacher has run an unusually well-funded campaign, raising roughly $13.7 million to Boebert's $1.2 million, though outside spending has been modest and slightly favors the incumbent. The two met in a single televised debate in October.\n\nThe only public poll, conducted in late September by a Democratic sponsor, showed Boebert ahead 45 to 40 among likely voters. Expert raters are split, with most calling the race Lean or Likely Republican and three rating it a Tossup. Prediction markets give Democrats roughly a one-in-three chance. Boebert remains favored on the district's fundamentals, but the fundraising gap and national environment keep the race competitive.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1824, "margin": -5.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3343, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1945, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2743, "margin": -4.7}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2626, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.23, "margin": -4.7}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2582, "margin": -4.8}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2829, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2916, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2767, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3037, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.311, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.297, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2522, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-1